 ## Subtopics
 
-### GaussianBody
-Uses physical-based priors in canonical space to regularize Gaussians and avoid dynamic cloth artifacts. Choose when physical constraints are more effective than redesigned densification for cloth handling. [Link](9209-gaussianbody.md)
-
-### SplattingAvatar
-Embeds Gaussians onto a canonical human body mesh using barycentric coordinates and normal displacements. Choose when mesh-based representation is preferred for topology consistency. [Link](9556-splattingavatar.md)
-
-### Inpainting for Displaced Objects
-Uses generative models to fill missing information when objects are displaced. Choose when dealing with occlusions or missing data in the scene. [Link](9523-inpainting-for-displaced-objects.md)
+### Joint Human & Scene Optimization
+This variant optimizes human and scene Gaussians jointly. The human model acts as a constraint for the scene reconstruction, which helps mitigate floating Gaussians (floaters) that typically appear in areas around intersections or occlusions when using sparse input views. This approach contrasts with sequential optimization (scene first, then human) which is prone to such artifacts [S3].
 
